       "              {\n",
       "                \"text\": \"Identifying the \\\"top 5\\\" cricketers is always a bit subjective and can depend on current form, format (Test, ODI, T20), and individual preferences. However, based on consistent performance, impact, and overall skill across formats in recent times, here are five prominent Indian cricketers who are widely regarded among the best:\\n\\n1.  **Virat Kohli:** A modern legend, Virat Kohli is one of the most prolific run-scorers in all formats of the game. Known for his immaculate technique, aggressive batting, and ability to chase down targets, he holds numerous records and is widely considered one of the greatest batsmen of all time.\\n\\n2.  **Rohit Sharma:** The current captain of the Indian team in all formats, Rohit Sharma is a destructive opener, particularly in white-ball cricket where he holds the record for the most double centuries in ODIs. His elegant strokeplay and ability to score big make him a formidable force. He has also significantly improved his Test match batting.\\n\\n3.  **Jasprit Bumrah:** One of the world's leading fast bowlers across all formats, Jasprit Bumrah is known for his unique action, express pace, pinpoint yorkers, and deadly variations. He is a match-winner capable of picking up wickets at crucial junctures and is highly respected by batsmen globally.\\n\\n4.  **Ravindra Jadeja:** An exceptional all-rounder, Ravindra Jadeja excels in all three departments of the game. He is a left-arm orthodox spinner who can pick up wickets consistently, a dynamic left-handed middle-order batsman capable of quick runs, and arguably one of the best fielders in the world. His contributions provide immense balance to the team.\\n\\n5.  **Hardik Pandya:** A dynamic all-rounder, Hardik Pandya brings a unique blend of explosive batting, crucial medium-pace bowling, and electric fielding. He is a match-winner in white-ball cricket, capable of changing the momentum of a game with both bat and ball, and has also captained India in T20Is.\\n\\n**Honourable Mentions:**\\n*   **Rishabh Pant:** While currently injured, his match-winning abilities, especially in Test cricket, make him one of India's most exciting talents.\\n*   **Mohammed Shami/Mohammed Siraj:** Both are excellent pace bowlers, particularly potent in Test cricket, known for their ability to swing the ball and pick up crucial wickets.\\n*   **Ravichandran Ashwin:** A modern spin legend, especially in Test cricket, with an incredible record and a constantly evolving arsenal of variations.\\n*   **Shubman Gill:** A rising star who has shown immense potential and consistency across formats.\\n\\nThis list could easily change as new talents emerge and established stars continue to perform.\"\n",
